The monsters that have an AD_DRLI attack (drain levels) are:
vampires, vampire lords, Vlad the Impaler, barrow wights,
wraiths, Nazgul, and Demogorgon.  Succubi and incubi also do
if SEDUCE is not defined.

Note that level draining respects magic cancellation, so if
you have MC3 then it's not worth worrying about in the post-castle
game.  A level drain may very occasionally succeed, but you'll get 
that level back as soon as you kill something.  If you only
have MC2 (or less) then it may be worth switching to Excalibur
when fighting those monsters.

Any high-level spellcaster can curse your items; that includes
liches, nalfeshnees, titans, ki-rin, Archons, aligned and high 
priests, Orcus, Demogorgon, and the Wizard of Yendor.  (There's
a few others too, for instance, some of the quest nemeses.)  Also,
after you kill the Wizard, occasionally you'll be hit with a curse
items spell even when there are no monsters around. Magic
cancellation doesn't help here, so it's generally a good idea
to wield Magicbane to ward off curses when you don't specifically
need another weapon.


